* START-HISTORY:
* 28 Oct 26 dm  New (S.88 phase 2, S2).  The test that TOOL.BULK made of its undo file (check.undo), moved here so that TOOL.QUERY asks the same question of &queries& before it writes
*               or deletes a record.  TOOL.BULK's wording is kept (messages 12761 to 12764 say what its strings said).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_ownfile(fv, name, ok, why)
*
*     fv     the file, open, that the page has opened by its VOC name
*     name   the VOC name it was opened by (&queries&, &bulk.undo&): the name the file must carry on the disk
*     ok     returned: 1 when the page may write and delete records of fv, else 0
*     why    returned: null when ok; else the sentence that says why not (messages 12410 to 12412, 12518, 12519, 12761 to 12764)
*
*   WHY IT EXISTS.  A page is an $internal program, and the kernel's edit gates let $internal programs through, so a page that writes a file it opened by a name the
*   PERSON can point somewhere else (a VOC entry &queries& that is a pointer to the program file bp) would write the program file with only the VOC gate on.  The page therefore
*   asks for itself, and asks here, in one place, so that two pages cannot ask differently.  The file must be, all of these, or it is refused:
*
*     a dynamic file,
*     not read only,
*     standing DIRECTLY in this account's own directory (the folder the VOC is in) under exactly the name it was opened by - so a pointer to another account's file, to a dictionary
*     (dict/zq) or to bp is not one,
*     of K$EDIT.KIND 0 (not the VOC, a dictionary, a program file, nor a record or the structure of a file of the shared account), and
*     one the kernel's own edit rules (K$EDIT.OK of its pathname) allow this session to change.
*
*   The first reason found is returned; nothing is changed.  A refusal by the kernel's rules is shown in the kernel's own words (!edit_msg).
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_ownfile(fv, name, ok, why)
$catalog $tk_ownfile

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h

   deffun edit_msg(kind) calling '!edit_msg'

   ok = 0
   why = ''
   ucd = ''
   open 'VOC' to uvf then
      ucd = fileinfo(uvf, FL$PATH)
      close uvf
   end
   if ucd # '' then ucd = field(ucd, '/', 1, dcount(ucd, '/') - 1)         ;* the account's own directory: the folder the VOC is in
   ucp = fileinfo(fv, FL$PATH)
   uct = fileinfo(fv, FL$TYPE)
   ucek = kernel(K$EDIT.KIND, ucp)
   uceo = kernel(K$EDIT.OK, ucp)
   begin case
      case uct # FL$TYPE.DH
         why = sysmsg(12761, name)
      case fileinfo(fv, FL$READONLY) = 1
         why = sysmsg(12762, name)
      case ucd = '' or ucp # ucd : '/' : name
         why = sysmsg(12763, name)
      case ucek >= 1 and ucek <= 3
         why = sysmsg(12764, name, (if ucek = 1 then 'the VOC' else (if ucek = 2 then 'a dictionary' else 'a program file')))
      case not(uceo)
         why = edit_msg(ucek)                                   ;* the kernel's own words
      case ucek # 0
         why = edit_msg(ucek)                                   ;* a record or the structure of a shared file: the kernel's words for it (not reached from the account's own directory, kept as a floor)
      case 1
         ok = 1
   end case

   return
end

* END-CODE
